1350 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Kali emerged from an Integrated Design Project \050IDP\051\054 where the objective was to identify real\055world problems and develop meaningful design\055led solutions\056 Through research\054 we explored the environmental impact of weddings\054 particularly the large amount of floral\054 food\054 and decorative waste generated during celebrations\056 While weddings are joyful and culturally significant\054 they often contribute to excessive waste\054 creating an opportunity to rethink traditional practices through sustainable alternatives\056\015\n\015\nResponding to this issue\054 Kali was envisioned as a hypothetical sustainable fashion brand that transforms discarded wedding flowers into eco\055printed textiles through natural dyeing and imprinting techniques\056 By experimenting with botanical waste\054 vegetable peels\054 and eco\055printing methods\054 the project explores how waste can be repurposed into meaningful keepsakes\054 promoting conscious consumption while giving celebrations a more sustainable afterlife\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 1351 0 R
     /Pg 1338 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

